{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And I will lay desolate, I, the land.</b> How so? 'And I will scatter you among the nations' — corresponding to 'and you shall dwell securely in your land,' and this is the seventh [year]." "<b>And your enemies shall be desolate upon it.</b> And so it says: 'all who pass by it shall be astonished and hiss at all its plagues.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The final clause 'והיא שביעית' is elliptical; read literally as 'and it is seventh-year.' The connection between the scattered inhabitants and the sabbatical year is left unstated."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:39.805628119Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}